<title>POLAND: Polish livestock headcount up in Q2, seen rising.</title>
<headline>Polish livestock headcount up in Q2, seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The headcount for Polish pigs and cattle rose by 1.3 and 0.2 percent respectively in the second quarter of 1997 and was 1.0 and 2.3 percent higher than a year ago, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>GUS said that in June Poland had 7.3 million cattle, including 3.49 million cows, and 18.15 million pigs. In April there was 7.28 million cattle and 17.91 million pigs.</p>
<p>GUS said that until October 30, some 9.8 percent of Polish farmers who owned cattle stock planned to increase their headcount, while 7.8 percent wanted to reduce it.</p>
<p>It said 22.2 percent wanted to increase their pig headcount in the period and that only 5.1 percent wanted to cut it.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
